{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.OrbitQuotientCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.OrbitQuotientCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.OrbitCount","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AtomWordShadow"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_invariant_functions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_invariant_functions","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L169-L186","doc":"**The `q = 1` Schur–Weyl trace, as a count.** A function `α → β` is invariant\nunder precomposition with `σ` exactly when it is constant on each orbit, so there are\n`(card β) ^ orbitCount σ` of them.\n\nWith `card β = 2` this is the `2^{c(σ)}` that `ClassicalTraceFloor`'s step 1 assumes:\n`σ` permuting the factors of `(ℂ²)^{⊗n}` fixes exactly the basis vectors constant on\neach cycle. 🛑 Identifying this count with a trace over an actual tensor power is a\nfurther step and is **not** in this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.eq_of_sameCycle_of_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.eq_of_sameCycle_of_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L161-L167","doc":"An invariant function is constant on each orbit. Routed through\n`SameCycle.exists_pow_eq'`, which supplies a **natural** power, so no `ℤ` induction is\nneeded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.apply_pow_eq_of_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.apply_pow_eq_of_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L153-L158","doc":"Invariance under `σ` propagates to every natural power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.card_quotient_sameCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.card_quotient_sameCycle","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L127-L150","doc":"**The bridge.** The number of orbits of `σ` — genuinely, as the cardinality of the\n`SameCycle` quotient — is `orbitCount σ`.\n\nMathlib has the setoid but nothing connecting it to `cycleType`; this is that\nconnection, and it is what makes `orbitCount` a count of orbits rather than a\n`cycleType` bookkeeping device. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.quotientSameCycleEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.quotientSameCycleEquiv","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L80-L125","doc":"**Every orbit is either a fixed point or a cycle factor.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.apply_cyclePoint_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.apply_cyclePoint_ne","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L75-L78","doc":"A cycle factor's chosen point is moved by `σ` itself, not merely by the factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.cyclePoint_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.cyclePoint_mem","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.cyclePoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.cyclePoint","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L65-L69","doc":"A point of a cycle factor's support. Choice is genuine: a cycle factor is a\ncycle, hence has nonempty support, but nothing picks a point for us. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fintypeQuotientSameCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fintypeQuotientSameCycle","kind":"instance","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/OrbitQuotientCount.lean#L60-L63","signatureChunk":0}]}